		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"### Legend\n\nCyan: curriculum hierarchy (module guide to lesson).\nBlue: lesson to atomic topic.\nGreen: topic grounds in a source record (each green edge reads \"grounded by\").\nOrange: uncertainty and limits.\nPurple: hypotheses and open questions.\n\nAn edge records a relationship in this library; it is never a causal claim.","x":0,"y":0,"width":460,"height":289,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"uncertainty","type":"text","text":"### Uncertainty\n\n- Concentration is a proxy for exposure\n- Dropout undercounts side effects\n- Mechanism knowledge is not clinical evidence","x":0,"y":609,"width":460,"height":154,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"hypothesis","type":"text","text":"### Open questions\n\n- How much variability in exposure comes from adherence versus metabolism?\n- How do downstream adaptations change a drug's effect over time?\n- What determines an individual's time to steady state beyond half-life?","x":0,"y":823,"width":460,"height":232,"color":"6"},
